From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:47:20 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: Improve with AI does what it's asked at once, says
 what it did; a redesign only when asked
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1.5.3's Improve ran every direction as a redesign: up to three rounds with
screenshots (50–90 s with a real AI), a brief that forbade hiding anything,
and a CSS check that took out every display: none. So «убери шортсы и
цифры у колокольчика» on YouTube took long, said "Designing… 1/3", and
hid neither: the shelf's display: none was taken out and its "hide" entry,
as the AI wrote it, was dropped.

- A direction ("убери шортсы", "hide the bell count", "bigger text",
  "dark") is done as asked in one quick round, as in 1.5.2: the page's
  outline (now with YouTube's is-* marks, as [is-shorts]), the boost's CSS
  and the direction go to the AI with a brief to do exactly that; no
  screenshot, no review. boost_ai::Classify picks it; a redesign in rounds
  only for an empty direction or one asking for it ("redesign", "редизайн",
  "переделай целиком", "сделай красиво", "make it beautiful"…).
- What it's asked to hide goes into "hide" with a label ("полку Shorts"),
  and the hiding rules of its CSS become zaps too; each is still checked
  (never html, body, main, a field or the content; :has() is fine unless it
  points at them) and checked on the page, a little more loosely as it was
  asked for by name. The rest of the CSS is checked as before: nothing from
  the internet, no scripts, no animations.
- It says what it's doing, in the person's language: "Смотрю страницу…",
  "Спрашиваю Claude Code… прочитал 812 элементов страницы", "Нашёл: …",
  then "Скрыл: полку Shorts, счётчик уведомлений · Изменил: …" in the
  editor and on the page's pill. Below it, the list of what changed: a
  click shows it on the page for a moment (outlined, scrolled to, a hidden
  one shown again), each with its own Undo.
- A redesign's rounds say what the last one changed ("Reviewing… 2/3 ·
  round 1: A dark, calm reading desk."), and "Enough, keep this" («Хватит,
  оставить так») in the editor and the pill stops it with what's on the
  page.

